  "description": "<p>This bug can be seen when trying to perform a PATCH request that includes the use of a RDF prefix that is undefined. The bug is that the body of the HTTP response to the client is an internal stacktrace. The fix should catch the exception, include a simple error message (e.g. \"RDF was not parsable: <span class=\"error\">&#91;line: 1, col: 4 &#93;</span> Unrecognized keyword: unknown\"), and a 400 response code.</p>\n\n<p>1. Create a resource<br/>\n$ curl -i -XPUT -H\"Content-Type: text/turtle\" -H'Link: &lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#BasicContainer\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#BasicContainer</a>&gt;;rel=\"type\"' --data-binary @body.ttl localhost:8080/rest/test0</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>Where @body.ttl is:<br/>\n```<br/>\n&lt;&gt; &lt;<a href=\"http://test.com#title\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://test.com#title</a>&gt; \"A Title\"<br/>\n```</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>2. Verify the new resource includes the triple found in body.ttl<br/>\n$ curl -i localhost:8080/rest/test0</p>\n\n<p>3. Perform PATCH<br/>\n$   512  curl -i -XPATCH -H\"Content-Type: application/sparql-update\" --data-binary @update.su localhost:8080/rest/test0</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>Where @update.su is:<br/>\n```<br/>\nDELETE \n{\r\n   &lt;&gt; unknown:title \"A Title\";\r\n}\n<p>INSERT </p>\n{\r\n   &lt;&gt; unknown:title \"new title\";\r\n}\n<p>WHERE {<br/>\n}<br/>\n```</p></li>\n</ul>\n",
